{"name":"Crunch Granola","hex":"#997a5a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crunch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To crush something, especially food, with a noisy crackling sound.","To be crushed with a noisy crackling sound."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A noisy crackling sound; the sound usually associated with crunching.\nCrunchiness.","Crunchiness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crunch"},{"term":"granola","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A breakfast and snack food consisting of loose, crispy pellets made of nuts, rolled oats, honey and other natural ingredients.","Ellipsis of crunchy granola."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Eating healthy food, supporting the protection of the environment, and having liberal views."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/granola"}],"entries":[{"title":"Granola","blocks":[{"text":"Granola is a food consisting of a mix of rolled oats, nuts, seeds, honey, and sometimes puffed rice that is usually baked with oil until crisp, toasted and golden brown, sometimes forming clumps. The mixture is stirred while baking to avoid burning and to maintain a loose breakfast cereal consistency. Dried fruit, such as raisins and dates, and confections such as chocolate are often added."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Granola%2C_yogurt%2C_fruit._%2816696981528%29.jpg/330px-Granola%2C_yogurt%2C_fruit._%2816696981528%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granola"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Granola_advertisement%2C_1893.png/500px-Granola_advertisement%2C_1893.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Granola_advertisement%2C_1893.png/500px-Granola_advertisement%2C_1893.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org